The application then answers at {{ APP_URL }}.

Everything the container writes into the project belongs to your host user — the
image maps its web user to the ids recorded in `.env`, so nothing here ever needs
`sudo`.

## Everyday commands

```bash
./{{ CLI_NAME }} migrate    # run pending migrations
./{{ CLI_NAME }} db:seed    # run seeders
./{{ CLI_NAME }} list       # every available command
./dockerbash                # a shell inside the container
{{ TEST_COMMAND }}          # the PHP test suite
```

